    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0641" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg507"/>

                <head>No. 361.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McLane to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 9, 1888</date>.
                        (Received February 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 543.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 472, of August 29,
                        1887,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d361-f1"/> concerning the facilities given in New
                    Caledonia to liberated convicts to proceed to the United States, I have the
                    honor of sending herewith a copy and translation of a note received through the
                    minister of the navy and the colonies from the governor of New Caledonia.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert
                        McLane.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d361-a1.xml" xpointer="d361-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
